Time zone sources for root/locale
=================================

`cargo xtask timezones` reads these files and writes root/locale: one
file for each line of `zones`, in the format Inferno's daytime(2)
reads, a README (`README.locale`), and `timezone`, the default (GMT).
The output is committed; the xtask test `locale_is_current` makes it
again and compares, so `cargo test --workspace` checks it on every
host. See docs/graphics.md, Section 11.4, and xtask/src/tz.rs.

africa, asia, australasia, backward, etcetera, europe, northamerica,
southamerica, LICENSE and version are from the IANA time zone database,
release 2026f (2026-10-28), https://data.iana.org/time-zones/releases/tzdata2026f.tar.gz
